Z||000000||85 gt fiero||12-07-2001||04:12 PM||||I just got done installing a new alternator in my 85 gt, and when i go to start it i hear the fuel pump turn on and i crank it and every so often it will pop like its going to start but it just keeps on cranking and then i let it set a few minutes and try it again and it will sound likes its firing but will stop and keep cranking over. The fuel tank is half full so theres plenty of gas and i tried spraying either in the throtle body(v6) and it fired a little more but no success.  Any help would be greatly appreciaed.  And buy the way i installed one a few weeks back but i found out that it was too a bad one so i installed this one. and its good.   Randy<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-07-2001||04:18 PM||||Make sure that all your connections are tight and check the wires to the coil. You may have unplugged it in the process.||||reg||1
Z||000002||85 gt fiero||12-07-2001||05:27 PM||||all the wires are in place and all the bolts tight.  i dont knowwhats wrong with it any more suggestions.  Randy thanx<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||12-07-2001||06:03 PM||||Just a thought - did your fuel injectors get unplugged, or more likely, did you blow a fuel injection fuse (in the fuse box under the dash)?<P>I'm thinking if the "main" injectors aren't getting their signals to squirt, then the only place you'd get fuel is from the cold start injector... which quits as soon as you stop cranking the starter.  Just a guess!||||reg||3
